        {
            "name": "[Lytbox] Project Management SOP",
            "content": "<h1>Project Management SOP</h1>\n<h2>1. Purpose</h2>\n<p>This SOP defines the exact steps required to manage a web design project from kickoff to completion.</p>\n<p>This system ensures:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clear scope control</li>\n<li>Transparent communication</li>\n<li>Structured milestone approvals</li>\n<li>Clean internal delegation</li>\n<li>No chaos, no guesswork</li>\n<li>The Project Page is the single source of truth.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Core Rule</h3>\n<p>All project activity must be documented inside:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Project Management Page</li>\n<li>The Client Dashboard</li>\n<li>The Milestone Approval section</li>\n<li>No project decisions live in DMs, Slack threads, or memory.</li>\n<li>If it is not documented, it does not exist.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Project Initialization</h3>\n<p>Responsible: Project Manager</p>\n<h4>3.1 Create the Project</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Duplicate the Project Starter Template</li>\n<li>Rename: Client Name – Project Name</li>\n<li>Assign internal team members</li>\n<li>Confirm timeline</li>\n<li>Confirm deliverables</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>3.2 Confirm Scope</h4>\n<p>Before work begins:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Review signed proposal</li>\n<li>Review deliverables</li>\n<li>Confirm milestone structure</li>\n<li>Confirm payment structure</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No assumptions. No verbal changes.</p>\n<h3>4. Client Dashboard Setup</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsible: Project Manager</li>\n<li>Confirm Client Dashboard is prepared</li>\n<li>Confirm deliverables checklist is visible</li>\n<li>Confirm milestone approval workflow is visible</li>\n<li>Confirm communication instructions are clear</li>\n<li>The Client Dashboard is the transparency layer.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Asset Collection</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsible: PM or VA</li>\n<li>Request branding assets</li>\n<li>Request content</li>\n<li>Request required access credentials</li>\n<li>Confirm everything is received before design begins</li>\n<li>Design does not begin without required assets.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. Design Phase</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsible: Designer</li>\n<li>Follow the defined Web Design Process</li>\n<li>Upload previews to Client Dashboard</li>\n<li>Request feedback through the dashboard only</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Rules:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All feedback must be written and documented</li>\n<li>Scope creep must be flagged immediately</li>\n<li>Revisions are limited to agreed scope</li>\n<li>No milestone moves forward without approval.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>7. Milestone Approval Workflow</h3>\n<p>Responsible: Project Manager</p>\n<p>Before moving to the next stage:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Present milestone deliverable</li>\n<li>Request written approval</li>\n<li>Mark milestone as approved</li>\n<li>Log approval date</li>\n<li>Development does not begin without approved design.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>8. Development Phase</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsible: Developer</li>\n<li>Build only from approved designs</li>\n<li>No creative deviations</li>\n<li>QA functionality</li>\n<li>Optimize performance</li>\n<li>Prepare staging link</li>\n<li>All progress is documented inside the Project Page.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. Final Review &amp; Launch</h3>\n<p>Responsible: PM + Developer</p>\n<p>Before launch:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Complete QA checklist</li>\n<li>Request final approval</li>\n<li>Confirm final payment received</li>\n<li>Schedule launch</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No launch without:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Final written approval</li>\n<li>Final payment received</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>10. Project Closure</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsible: PM or VA</li>\n<li>Deliver final files</li>\n<li>Confirm handoff</li>\n<li>Archive project</li>\n<li>Update status</li>\n<li>Request testimonial (optional)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>11. Non-Negotiables</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No work outside defined scope</li>\n<li>No skipped milestones</li>\n<li>No launch without final payment</li>\n<li>No undocumented approvals</li>\n<li>No unmanaged scope creep</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>12. Role Clarity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Project Manager</li>\n<li>Oversees process</li>\n<li>Protects scope</li>\n<li>Manages approvals</li>\n<li>Controls communication</li>\n<li>Designer</li>\n<li>Executes design phase</li>\n<li>Submits work for review</li>\n<li>Stays within scope</li>\n<li>Developer</li>\n<li>Builds approved designs only</li>\n<li>QA before submission</li>\n<li>No independent design decisions</li>\n<li>VA</li>\n<li>Collects assets</li>\n<li>Manages documentation</li>\n<li>Updates status</li>\n<li>Supports organization</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This system exists for one reason:</p>\n<p>To make every project repeatable, scalable, and delegatable.</p>"
        },
        {
            "name": "[Lytbox] Project Delivery SOP",
            "content": "<h1>Project Delivery SOP</h1>\n<h4>Design &amp; Development Workflow</h4>\n<p>This SOP governs the final stages of the web design and development process. It begins at internal Quality Control and ends after the 30-Day Support window is complete.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>This document must be followed by the assigned Designer, Developer, Project Manager, or VA responsible for delivery.</li>\n<li>No project is considered complete until every phase below is executed and documented inside the Project Dashboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1. Quality Control (Internal Only)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Goal: Internal perfection before the client sees the website.</li>\n<li>Quality Control must be completed in full before the project moves into Client Review or Launch preparation.</li>\n<li>The assigned Developer is responsible for executing the checklist.</li>\n<li>The Designer reviews visual consistency.</li>\n<li>The Project Manager gives final approval.</li>\n<li>All approvals must be documented inside the project.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.1 Structure &amp; UI</h3>\n<p>Confirm the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Spacing is consistent across all pages</li>\n<li>Typography is consistent and follows the brand system</li>\n<li>Buttons are styled consistently</li>\n<li>Hover states are applied where required</li>\n<li>No placeholder content remains anywhere on the site</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.2 Functionality</h3>\n<p>Confirm the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All internal and external links function correctly</li>\n<li>All forms are tested on the front end</li>\n<li>Form submissions are confirmed on the back end</li>\n<li>Error and success messages display correctly</li>\n<li>Mobile responsiveness is verified</li>\n<li>Tablet responsiveness is verified</li>\n<li>All project-specific features and integrations are tested</li>\n<li>If additional functions exist for the project, they must be listed and tested individually.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.3 Performance</h3>\n<p>Confirm the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Caching is active and functioning</li>\n<li>Images are optimized</li>\n<li>Lazy loading is enabled where appropriate</li>\n<li>PageSpeed testing has been performed</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.4 Technical</h3>\n<p>Confirm the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Favicon is installed</li>\n<li>404 page exists and works</li>\n<li>Privacy Policy page is linked</li>\n<li>SEO titles and meta descriptions are added</li>\n<li>Sitemap is generated</li>\n<li>SEO is tested at a basic level</li>\n<li>Accessibility is tested at a basic level</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>1.5 Final Internal Sign-Off</h3>\n<p>Before proceeding, the following approvals must be documented:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Designer approval</li>\n<li>Developer approval</li>\n<li>Project Manager approval</li>\n<li>The project may not move forward without all three.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Project Completion and Launch</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Goal: Ensure the website is 100 percent ready to go live.</li>\n<li>This phase begins only after Quality Control is completed and approved.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.1 Pre-Launch Checklist</h3>\n<p>Confirm the following before launch:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Final full backup is created</li>\n<li>DNS settings are prepared</li>\n<li>Production environment is ready</li>\n<li>Final payment has been received in full</li>\n<li>Client approval is documented in writing</li>\n<li>Rule: The site does not go live until payment has cleared.</li>\n<li>If payment has not been received, launch is paused.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.2 Launch Procedure</h3>\n<p>Once pre-launch conditions are satisfied:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Push the website to production</li>\n<li>Test the live domain</li>\n<li>Re-test all forms</li>\n<li>Re-test payments if applicable</li>\n<li>Confirm tracking scripts are functioning</li>\n<li>Document successful launch inside the Project Dashboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Handover Process</h2>\n<p>Goal: Transfer the completed website to the client in a professional and controlled manner.</p>\n<p>Handover occurs only after:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Website is live</li>\n<li>Final payment is confirmed</li>\n<li>No credentials are provided before payment is received in full.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3.1 Credential Delivery</h3>\n<p>Provide access securely. This may include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress login</li>\n<li>Hosting login</li>\n<li>Domain login</li>\n<li>Third-party tools included in the project</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Credentials must be transferred using a secure method. Do not send passwords in plain text email.</p>\n<h3>3.2 Documentation</h3>\n<p>Provide the following if included in scope:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Video walkthrough of the website</li>\n<li>Basic instructions for content updates</li>\n<li>Style guide</li>\n<li>Hosting or maintenance clarification</li>\n<li>Documentation should be concise and practical.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3.3 Ownership Confirmation</h3>\n<p>Confirm in writing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ownership transfer status</li>\n<li>Hosting arrangement</li>\n<li>Maintenance plan status</li>\n<li>If a maintenance plan is declined, this must be documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. 30-Day Support Window</h2>\n<p>Goal: Provide limited post-launch support for stability and minor corrections.</p>\n<h3>4.1 Activation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Document the support start date</li>\n<li>Confirm official support communication channel</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4.2 Support Scope</h3>\n<p>Included:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor bug fixes</li>\n<li>Technical corrections</li>\n<li>Small clarifications</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Not included:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>New features</li>\n<li>New pages</li>\n<li>Redesigns</li>\n<li>Strategy changes</li>\n<li>Out-of-scope requests require a new estimate and approval.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4.3 Project Closeout</h3>\n<p>At the end of the 30-day period:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm project is officially closed</li>\n<li>Offer maintenance plan if not already active</li>\n<li>Archive project documentation internally</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Enforcement Rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No client review before internal Quality Control approval.</li>\n<li>No launch before final payment is received.</li>\n<li>No credential transfer before payment is confirmed.</li>\n<li>All approvals must be documented.</li>\n<li>Scope boundaries must be enforced.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This SOP protects quality, revenue, and professionalism. It must be followed exactly for every project.</p>"
        },
